  "level": 9,
  "order": 904,
  "theme": "news",
  "culturalNote": "Kenya's weather news often has two stories at once: floods (mafuriko) in the west, where rivers like the Nzoia burst their banks around Budalang'i, and drought (ukame) in the north, where herders lose their livestock. Kenyans respond with \"harambee\" — pulling together money through churches, chamas and M-Pesa. Conversations like this one are full of \"kwamba\" (that), continuous tenses and \"jinsi … -vyo-\" (the way, as much as).",
  "startingPoint": "Evening at the kiosk near your flat. Mzee Kipchoge is reading the Daily Nation with a worried face.",
